WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:05.492
Technical OSINT is the analysis of lawfully accessible public information about internet-facing infrastructure.

00:00:05.492 --> 00:00:10.055
Its sources can include domains, DNS records, internet addresses, certificates, websites,

00:00:10.055 --> 00:00:13.788
public repositories, package registries, cloud references, and technical metadata.

00:00:13.788 --> 00:00:16.691
The work is analytical rather than intrusive.

00:00:16.691 --> 00:00:21.254
Analysts collect observable records, preserve dates and source context, compare indicators,

00:00:21.254 --> 00:00:22.913
and develop cautious judgments.

00:00:22.913 --> 00:00:27.475
Technical OSINT does not authorize scanning beyond approved limits, attempting access,

00:00:27.475 --> 00:00:29.964
using exposed credentials, or bypassing controls.

00:00:29.964 --> 00:00:33.282
Defenders use technical OSINT to improve attack-surface awareness,

00:00:33.282 --> 00:00:37.845
identify unknown or stale assets, support threat intelligence, assess vendor dependencies,

00:00:37.845 --> 00:00:40.333
and add public context during incidents.

00:00:40.333 --> 00:00:44.066
It can reveal questions that internal inventories should answer.

00:00:44.066 --> 00:00:46.970
Public records rarely tell the whole story.

00:00:46.970 --> 00:00:50.288
A domain may be parked, delegated, or abandoned.

00:00:50.288 --> 00:00:54.850
An address may belong to a cloud provider or shared host.

00:00:54.850 --> 00:00:59.828
A certificate may show that a name was validated at one time

00:00:59.828 --> 00:01:02.316
without proving current ownership or security.

00:01:02.316 --> 00:01:04.805
Strong analysis separates observation from inference.

00:01:04.805 --> 00:01:05.634
For example,

00:01:05.634 --> 00:01:11.441
a certificate record can support that a certificate covered a hostname on a date.

00:01:11.441 --> 00:01:17.663
Connecting that hostname to an organization or active system requires additional evidence and confidence language.

00:01:17.663 --> 00:01:20.981
The goal is responsible visibility and decision support.

00:01:20.981 --> 00:01:24.299
Work from an authorized scope, minimize unnecessary collection,

00:01:24.299 --> 00:01:27.617
document every important source, validate across independent evidence,

00:01:27.617 --> 00:01:32.180
and report risk signals as signals rather than claims of compromise.
